    <div class="section-eyebrow">SCIENCE TARGETS · 科学目标</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">These are within Redbank III's reach</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">
      The images below are from NASA/ESA/CSA's Hubble and James Webb Space Telescopes (public domain). Redbank III's 8-16 unit array can image fainter versions of these same targets — not this quality, but the same sky.
    </p>
    <div class="science-grid">
      <div class="science-card">
        <img src={`${imgBase}/images/targets/andromeda-hst.jpg`} alt="Andromeda Galaxy (Hubble)" loading="lazy">
        <div class="science-card-overlay">
          <h3>Andromeda Galaxy M31</h3>
          <p>A 4-unit Redbank III array resolves the galactic disk and faint stellar halo. 8 units approach Dragonfly's low-surface-brightness survey depth.</p>
          <div class="credit">NASA/ESA Hubble Space Telescope</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="science-card">
        <img src={`${imgBase}/images/targets/orion-hst.jpg`} alt="Orion Nebula (Hubble)" loading="lazy">
        <div class="science-card-overlay">
          <h3>Orion Nebula M42</h3>
          <p>A single Redbank III unit captures a satisfying M42. Array stacking reveals the faint outer gas shells.</p>
          <div class="credit">NASA/ESA Hubble Space Telescope</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="science-card">
        <img src={`${imgBase}/images/targets/horsehead-hst.jpg`} alt="Horsehead Nebula (Hubble)" loading="lazy">
        <div class="science-card-overlay">
          <h3>Horsehead Nebula Barnard 33</h3>
          <p>A classic dark nebula target. Requires 8+ units and long-exposure stacking to separate from light-polluted backgrounds.</p>
          <div class="credit">NASA/ESA Hubble Space Telescope</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="science-card">
        <img src={`${imgBase}/images/targets/pillars-hst.jpg`} alt="Pillars of Creation (Hubble)" loading="lazy">
        <div class="science-card-overlay">
          <h3>Pillars of Creation (Eagle Nebula M16)</h3>
          <p>Hubble's most iconic target. A 16-unit Redbank III array can capture the pillar structure's outline.</p>
          <div class="credit">NASA/ESA/CSA Hubble Space Telescope</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

